# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# INTERNAL — never published
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The working documents for this project are proprietary. Design notes, the
# decision record, the build plan, the current status, the per-vendor research and
# the submission analysis all stay on the machines they were written on.
#
# A separate, written-for-the-purpose public set will be produced when there is
# something for it to describe. Internal notes are not that, and a repository that
# will one day be public must never have carried them, not even in an old commit.
docs/
private/
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG.md

# The credential research — real measured limits, which vendors were rejected and
# why, which demand a payment card — lives in docs/research/ and is covered by the
# docs/ rule above. That is stack research and it stays ours.
#
# .env.example is the other half of that split and it IS published: the same 40
# credential names, one plain line each saying what it is for and where to get it.
# Three challenges require that a stranger can clone this and know what to obtain,
# and that requirement asks only "which credentials do I need" — nothing more.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TWO THINGS THAT MUST BE PUBLIC, AND ONE THAT MUST NEVER BE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The attestation keypair signs the head of our record. The PUBLIC half is
# committed on purpose: it is what lets anyone check our record without asking us
# for anything. A verifier that loaded its key from the file it was checking would
# prove nothing at all. The PRIVATE half never leaves one machine — the *.pem and
# *.key rules below cover it, and scripts/git-check.mjs proves it every run.
keys/*
!keys/*.pub
# And the file explaining all of the above. A public key with no explanation of
# why it is public is worse than useless — the person checking our record needs to
# read why the key lives outside the thing it verifies.
!keys/README.md

# Recorded real vendor responses. Committed on purpose: they are what lets a
# stranger clone this and run the whole thing end to end with no accounts and no
# keys. Three of the challenges we enter require exactly that.
#
# The recorder redacts credentials before writing, and scripts/git-check.mjs
# independently searches every one of these files for every real value in .env
# before any commit. Two mechanisms, because one would be a hope.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — nothing here is ever committed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The pattern is deliberately wide. A narrower one missed a file called .env.backup
# that contained real values. Wide is the only version that cannot be defeated by a
# filename nobody predicted.
.env*

# The one exception, and it holds no values — only the names of the credentials a
# stranger needs to obtain. Every real value lives in .env, which the rule above
# still catches. scripts/git-check.mjs searches this file for every real value in
# .env on every run, so the exception cannot quietly become a leak.
!.env.example

# Private keys, certificates, and anything holding one.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BUILD OUTPUT AND DEPENDENCIES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEST AND TOOL OUTPUT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

.cache/
.charter-cache/

# Generated PDFs, packs and downloads from real runs. These can contain data from
# whatever was fed into a run, so they are never committed.
tmp/
scratch/
*.local.pdf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RESEARCH AND TOOL OUTPUT — other people's pages, not ours to republish
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Automated browsing leaves copies of the pages it read on disk. Those are other
# companies' content. Publishing them would be both useless and not ours to do.
.playwright-mcp/
*-vars.txt
*.har
snapshots/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL TOOLING AND EDITOR STATE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.veris/
.vercel/
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPERATING SYSTEM CLUTTER
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
site/run.json
